  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 4,
        "rationale": "Four findings are genuinely fixed (gh run watch now runs directly with --exit-status so set -e sees it, grep -q reads a here-string, the gh api failure exits with an error instead of || true, and the identity is passed via `git -c user.email=... commit` on the commit itself so it is in effect before the commit), but the jq dependency is still unguaranteed and a second jq call was added, and no commit.gpgsign defense exists, so three objective checks for skill-covered findings fail (jq-guaranteed-or-replaced, version-read-does-not-depend-on-unguarded-jq, commit-signing-safe-for-ci) and the cap of 4 applies."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 2,
        "rationale": "The decoy `rm -f \"$tmp_response\" || true` line was deleted (decoy-optional-cleanup-untouched fails, capping at 4), and the agent also rewrote far beyond the review's scope: README edits, a new 119-line test suite, workflow concurrency/GH_TOKEN/step gating, a GITHUB_REF branch guard, version-format validation, sed-to-jq rewrite, PUBLISH_RUN_ID validation, and post-push verification; only the `set -euo pipefail` decoy survived."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 6,
        "rationale": "The reply names the real failure modes for the fixes it made (exit status discarded inside `< <(... | tail)`, pipefail/SIGPIPE killing echo on a >64 KiB log, gh api printing the error body to stdout with || true keeping it, no git identity on a runner), but it says nothing at all about the unguaranteed jq dependency or commit.gpgsign, and the process-substitution explanation never states that the subshell is invisible to set -e."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 4.199999999999999
  },
